<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Furs of Valencia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1261</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">Furs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> were the law code of the Kingdom of Valencia, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> swore as the realm's general law in 1261. Based largely on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> and later written in Catalan, they were extended by later kings and the Valencian Corts. They were abolished by Philip V's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta decrees</a> in 1707.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/furs-of-valencia.jpg" alt="Furs of Valencia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joanbanjo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FORI_REGNI_Valentiae,_Furs_de_Val%C3%A8ncia_1547.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
